class Node {
    int data;
    Node left;
    Node right;

    Node(int val) {
        data = val;
        left = right = null;
    }
}

class Solution {
    Node prev = null, first = null, second = null;

    public Node correctBST(Node root) {
        find(root);                                     // start inorder scan

        int temp = first.data;
        first.data = second.data;
        second.data = temp;                             // swap back values

        return root;
    }

    void find(Node root) {
        if (root == null) return;

        find(root.left);                                // visit left

        if (prev != null && root.data < prev.data) {     // order broken
            if (first == null) {
                first = prev;                             // first bad node
            }
            second = root;                                // second bad node
        }

        prev = root;                                     // move prev ahead
        find(root.right);                                 // visit right
    }
}

//////////////////////// DRY RUN /////////////////////////////

Input tree

            10
           /  \
          5    8
         / \
        2   20

Inorder walk: 2, 5, 20, 8, 10

2   prev=null        skip
5   prev=2           ok
20  prev=5           ok
8   prev=20          8 < 20  -> first=20, second=8
10  prev=8           ok

Swap first and second: 20 <-> 8

Corrected tree

            10
           /  \
          5    20
         / \
        2    8

//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Fixing Two Nodes of BST

Given the root of a Binary Search Tree (BST), where exactly two nodes have been swapped by mistake, restore the BST by swapping the values of the misplaced nodes.
Return the root of the corrected BST.

Note: It is guaranteed that exactly two nodes have been swapped, and restoring their values will make the tree a valid BST. The structure of the tree must remain unchanged.

Examples:
````````````````````````````````````````````````````````````````
Input: root = [10, 5, 8, 2, 20]

Output: [10, 5, 20, 2, 8]

Explanation: The nodes 20 and 8 were swapped.

Input tree

            10
           /  \
          5    8
         / \
        2   20

Output tree

            10
           /  \
          5    20
         / \
        2    8

````````````````````````````````````````````````````````````````````
Input: root = [5, 10, 20, 2, 8]

Output: [10, 5, 20, 2, 8]

Explanation: The nodes 10 and 5 were swapped.

Input tree

            5
           /  \
         10    20
        /  \
       2    8

Output tree

            10
           /  \
          5    20
         / \
        2    8

``````````````````````````````````````````````````````````````````````

Constraints:
2 ≤ Number of nodes ≤ 10^5
1 ≤ root[i] ≤ 10^7

